---
description: Figure creation
alwaysApply: false
---
All figures must follow publication-quality styling.

Defaults:
- consistent font family and sizes
- minimal, readable ticks (≤5 per axis)
- no excessive decimals
- uncluttered layout with adequate spacing

Prefer:
- vector output (SVG/PDF)
- clear axis labels with units
- restrained, colorblind-safe palettes

Avoid:
- crowded subplots
- default matplotlib styling
- unnecessary gridlines or spines

If a figure looks busy, simplify before adding detail.
Consistency across figures is more important than local optimization.